    stem: "Question 3 — International Environment. (A) Read the information supplied and answer the questions which follow.",
    questionText: "Calculate the Balance of Trade and the Balance of Payments using the data above. State whether your answer is a surplus or a deficit. Show your workings.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed","notation":"14 marks: BOT 6marks, BOP 8marks"}, totalMarks: 14,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "point", verbatim: "Visible Exports – Visible Imports", marks: 1, contextNote: "Balance of Trade. BOT 6marks in all: formula 1 mark and each correct figure 1 mark, € sign 1 mark, surplus/deficit 1 mark." },
    { id: "r-2", kind: "point", verbatim: "€ 72bn - € 34bn= € 38bn surplus", marks: 5, contextNote: "The scheme prints five separate marks along this line: € 72bn, € 34bn, € 38bn, the € sign and surplus." },
    { id: "r-3", kind: "point", verbatim: "Total Exports – Total Imports", marks: 1, contextNote: "Balance of Payments. BOP 8marks in all: formula 1 mark and each correct figure 1 mark, € sign 1 mark, surplus/deficit 1 mark." },
    { id: "r-4", kind: "point", verbatim: "(72bn+93bn) - (34bn+84bn) = €47bn surplus [Own Figure Allowed]", marks: 7, accepts: ["€165bn- €118bn = €47bn surplus [Own Figure Allowed]"], contextNote: "The scheme prints seven separate marks along this line: 72bn, 93bn, 34bn, 84bn, €47bn, the € sign and surplus. Own Figure Allowed: a figure carried forward from an earlier slip still earns them." },
    ],
