          "alt": "A ruled stimulus box headed, in bold, \"Ireland 2023 Q3\", containing a greyscale isometric infographic of Ireland's trade in that quarter. The graphic is built as two large overlapping rounded lobes on a mid-grey field, with a faint world-map/globe silhouette behind the left one. The left lobe is captioned \"Goods\" and shows two container ships loaded with stacked containers; the right lobe is captioned \"Services\" and shows two seated office workers at desks with laptops. Beneath each lobe are two value labels separated by a dotted vertical rule: under Goods, \"Exports €72bn\" and \"Imports €34bn\"; under Services, \"Exports €93bn\" and \"Imports €84bn\". Right-aligned below the graphic is the attribution \"Adapted from cso.ie\". It is an infographic, not a plotted chart — there are no axes and no scale; the four euro amounts are printed directly as labels and are fully legible.",
